\chapter{Module C: Acute Trauma}

\section{Overview}

Module C models the physiological disruption caused by acute trauma, including
shock states, perfusion deficits, inflammatory cascades, metabolic derangement,
and organ‑system instability. It integrates upstream signals from Modules A and B
and provides critical downstream influence on Module D (senescence) and the
countermeasure optimization engine.

The module captures:
\begin{itemize}
    \item hemodynamic instability,
    \item oxygen transport failure,
    \item lactate accumulation,
    \item inflammatory cytokine surge,
    \item multi‑organ stress response.
\end{itemize}

\section{State Variables}

The trauma physiology state vector is:
\[
\mathbf{S}_C(t)
=
\big(
H(t),\,
O(t),\,
L(t),\,
\iota(t),\,
M(t)
\big),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $H(t)$: hemodynamic stability index,
    \item $O(t)$: oxygenation efficiency,
    \item $L(t)$: lactate concentration,
    \item $\iota(t)$: inflammatory index,
    \item $M(t)$: metabolic stability.
\end{itemize}

\section{Hemodynamic Instability Model}

Hemodynamic collapse is modeled as:
\[
\frac{dH}{dt}
=
-\alpha_H S_{\text{inj}}
+
\beta_H O(t)
-
\delta_H H(t),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $S_{\text{inj}}$: trauma severity score,
    \item $\alpha_H$: injury‑driven hemodynamic loss,
    \item $\beta_H$: oxygenation‑driven recovery,
    \item $\delta_H$: decay constant.
\end{itemize}

\section{Oxygen Transport Dynamics}

Oxygenation efficiency:
\[
\frac{dO}{dt}
=
\gamma_O H(t)
-
\delta_O O(t)
+
\eta_O,
\]
where $\eta_O$ is baseline oxygenation.

Coupling to Module B:
\[
\gamma_O(t)
=
\gamma_O^{(0)}
-
\lambda_O P(t),
\]
reflecting pathogen‑induced hypoxia.

\section{Lactate Accumulation}

Lactate rises under hypoperfusion:
\[
\frac{dL}{dt}
=
\alpha_L
\Big(
\frac{1}{O(t) + \epsilon}
\Big)
+
\beta_L S_{\text{inj}}
-
\delta_L L(t),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\alpha_L$: hypoxia‑driven lactate production,
    \item $\beta_L$: trauma‑driven lactate production,
    \item $\delta_L$: lactate clearance.
\end{itemize}

\section{Inflammatory Cascade}

Inflammation index:
\[
\frac{d\iota}{dt}
=
\alpha_{\iota} S_{\text{inj}}
+
\beta_{\iota} P(t)
+
\gamma_{\iota} \sum_i g_i(t)
-
\delta_{\iota} \iota(t),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\beta_{\iota}$: pathogen‑driven inflammation (Module B),
    \item $\gamma_{\iota}$: genetic dysregulation‑driven inflammation (Module A).
\end{itemize}

\section{Metabolic Stability}

Metabolic stability:
\[
\frac{dM}{dt}
=
-\alpha_M L(t)
+
\beta_M O(t)
-
\delta_M M(t).
\]

